Build a thermochemical calculation from compatible data and a stated temperature range (@metal-thermochemical: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @metals-and-metallurgical-production, #source "../../../chemistry/general-chemistry/sources/NIST-JANAF.lingua#r_64N7R6GQB5B7NVW5KBXB3NYD44", #source "../sources/Metallurgical-Material-and-Heat-Balances-NPTEL.lingua#r_38NWQRDJH3RVM3NNGB71RR1X43", #source "../sources/Phase-Transitions-Bhadeshia-Yan.lingua#r_2PMPJ2B4GPGDT62S567TX1DCPJ", #metals-and-metallurgical-production "../balances/Heat-work-reaction-enthalpy-and-furnace-accounts.lingua#r_685N41C1X9JPJKRZRMF2PYACFE") { r_3EKZWFQG2VPXAKR9QZQ81JYSF1
**Read:** [NIST-JANAF Thermochemical Tables — fourth-edition reference data](../../../chemistry/general-chemistry/sources/NIST-JANAF.lingua#r_64N7R6GQB5B7NVW5KBXB3NYD44), the full table definitions, data basis, and complete relevant original evaluation; [Materials, energy, and heat balances in metallurgical processes — Satish Ch. Koria](../sources/Metallurgical-Material-and-Heat-Balances-NPTEL.lingua#r_38NWQRDJH3RVM3NNGB71RR1X43), the complete thermochemistry and worked metal-extraction sequence; [Phase Transitions — Bhadeshia and Yan](../sources/Phase-Transitions-Bhadeshia-Yan.lingua#r_2PMPJ2B4GPGDT62S567TX1DCPJ), the full elementary thermodynamics and equilibrium treatment.

Identify each species/phase, reaction, reference state, and data source before combining thermochemical values. Standard enthalpy, Gibbs energy, heat capacity, entropy, phase transitions, and activities play different roles. A tabulated value at one temperature is not a complete high-temperature process model.

Derive temperature corrections from the appropriate heat-capacity and phase-transition account, retaining the actual validity range. Reaction data normalized on different amounts or oxygen bases need conversion before comparison. Distinguish an evaluated data set, an assessed solution model, a measured property, and an extrapolated estimate.

Keep numerical and thermodynamic uncertainty separate from feed and operating variability. Correlated reference-data/model errors may persist across many calculations. Agreement between two programs using the same data does not independently validate that data or the phase assumptions.

**Work:** reproduce a substantial temperature-dependent extraction/refining equilibrium or heat calculation using its exact data and references. Independently check units, reaction balance, reference-state conversion, phase transitions, and a limiting case. Compare an alternative defensible data/model source and identify where the engineering conclusion changes. Report the evidence needed to resolve the discrepancy rather than selecting whichever value supports the preferred route.

**Continue:** [Join material and energy balances with actual phases, temperatures, and work](../balances/Heat-work-reaction-enthalpy-and-furnace-accounts.lingua#r_685N41C1X9JPJKRZRMF2PYACFE).

